WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.243 --> 00:00:02.042
- Good morning Believe Nation, it's Evan.

00:00:02.042 --> 00:00:03.714
My one word is believe in,

00:00:03.714 --> 00:00:05.055
and I believe in people more

00:00:05.055 --> 00:00:06.348
than they believe in themselves.

00:00:06.348 --> 00:00:09.120
And my sincere hope that
if you see in yourself

00:00:09.120 --> 00:00:12.507
what I see in you, you'll be
able to change the planet.

00:00:12.507 --> 00:00:16.136
So to help you on your journey,
today's message is show up.

00:00:16.136 --> 00:00:17.897
Over to you Brene Brown.

00:00:17.897 --> 00:00:20.405
(rooster crows)

00:00:20.405 --> 00:00:22.504
♫ I wake up every morning

00:00:22.504 --> 00:00:24.919
♫ Espresso keep me a going

00:00:24.919 --> 00:00:28.419
♫ I wake up every morning

00:00:29.616 --> 00:00:32.037
- My story is that I am a researcher

00:00:32.037 --> 00:00:34.392
and I never thought I would
have a big public career.

00:00:34.392 --> 00:00:38.788
And so I did a Ted talk
that went very viral

00:00:38.788 --> 00:00:40.788
and in the wake of that,

00:00:42.554 --> 00:00:44.876
I was kind of everywhere
for a couple of months

00:00:44.876 --> 00:00:48.459
on every CNN.com, in
PR, it was everywhere,

00:00:49.344 --> 00:00:51.531
and something that I wasn't used to.

00:00:51.531 --> 00:00:54.996
And the marching orders from my therapist

00:00:54.996 --> 00:00:58.174
and my husband were do not
read the comments online.

00:00:58.174 --> 00:00:59.659
(audience laughs)

00:00:59.659 --> 00:01:02.492
So I read all the comments online.

00:01:04.552 --> 00:01:08.474
And so one morning I woke up
and there were two or three

00:01:08.474 --> 00:01:12.611
new articles out and I
started reading the comments.

00:01:12.611 --> 00:01:14.931
And they were devastating.

00:01:14.931 --> 00:01:16.778
They weren't about my
work, they were about me,

00:01:16.778 --> 00:01:18.735
they were super personal.

00:01:18.735 --> 00:01:21.152
And they were the things that

00:01:23.218 --> 00:01:26.161
creative people play in their mind

00:01:26.161 --> 00:01:29.081
and then give up doing what
they really want to do.

00:01:29.081 --> 00:01:32.690
Like if I asked every single one of you,

00:01:32.690 --> 00:01:35.190
what would you try if you knew

00:01:36.564 --> 00:01:39.613
people would never say this about you?

00:01:39.613 --> 00:01:41.196
What would this be?

00:01:42.214 --> 00:01:44.577
Those were the comments that morning.

00:01:44.577 --> 00:01:46.742
Of course, she embraces imperfection,

00:01:46.742 --> 00:01:47.901
what choice does she have?

00:01:47.901 --> 00:01:49.734
Look at how she looks.

00:01:50.670 --> 00:01:53.083
I feel sorry for her kids.

00:01:53.083 --> 00:01:55.166
Less research more Botox.

00:01:56.821 --> 00:01:58.557
Just mean personal attacks,

00:01:58.557 --> 00:02:02.474
the things that really
up until that moment had

00:02:06.293 --> 00:02:10.674
inspired me to stay very small
in my life and in my career.

00:02:10.674 --> 00:02:13.499
Just so I could avoid those things.

00:02:13.499 --> 00:02:17.301
So that morning, Steve and
the kids leave, I stay home.

00:02:17.301 --> 00:02:19.509
I get on the couch

00:02:19.509 --> 00:02:21.504
and I watch eight hours of Downtown Abbey.

00:02:21.504 --> 00:02:23.917
(audience laughs)

00:02:23.917 --> 00:02:27.367
And when it's over, I don't
want to turn off Downtown Abbey,

00:02:27.367 --> 00:02:29.534
'cause the minute you
turn off Downtown Abbey,

00:02:29.534 --> 00:02:31.493
then it's like soccer practice and dinner

00:02:31.493 --> 00:02:35.397
and back to the mean people,
and maybe should I get Botox?

00:02:35.397 --> 00:02:39.564
Maybe, you know, maybe if
I stand still when I talk.

00:02:40.668 --> 00:02:43.435
So I get out my laptop and I do a search

00:02:43.435 --> 00:02:45.235
for who was president in the United States

00:02:45.235 --> 00:02:47.262
during the Downtown Abbey era.

00:02:47.262 --> 00:02:48.977
Have you ever done that,
like you're numbing with TV

00:02:48.977 --> 00:02:51.042
or a movie and so when
it's over, you just like,

00:02:51.042 --> 00:02:52.644
you stay in that space by learning more

00:02:52.644 --> 00:02:55.380
about the actors and what's going on?

00:02:55.380 --> 00:02:58.414
I've been doing this long enough to know

00:02:58.414 --> 00:03:00.485
that this is like you're
laughing with me not at me.

00:03:00.485 --> 00:03:02.346
(audience laughs)

00:03:02.346 --> 00:03:05.245
And so I put it in and
Theodore Roosevelt comes up

00:03:05.245 --> 00:03:08.245
and a quote comes up, and I read it.

00:03:09.502 --> 00:03:10.562
And this is what it says.

00:03:10.562 --> 00:03:12.312
It's a quote from a speech that he gave

00:03:12.312 --> 00:03:13.904
in the early 1900s at the Sorbonne,

00:03:13.904 --> 00:03:17.803
and a lot of people call it
The Man in the Arena Speech.

00:03:17.803 --> 00:03:21.767
And this is the passage
that changes my life.

00:03:21.767 --> 00:03:24.534
"It's not the critic who counts,

00:03:24.534 --> 00:03:27.375
"it's not the man who points
out how the strong man stumbles

00:03:27.375 --> 00:03:30.016
"or where the doer of deeds
could've done it better,

00:03:30.016 --> 00:03:31.384
"the credit belongs to the person

00:03:31.384 --> 00:03:33.333
"who's actually in the arena

00:03:33.333 --> 00:03:36.762
"whose face is marred with
blood and sweat and dust,

00:03:36.762 --> 00:03:40.924
"who at the best, in the
end, knows the triumph

00:03:40.924 --> 00:03:43.689
"of high achievement and who at worst,

00:03:43.689 --> 00:03:46.939
"if he fails, he fails daring greatly."

00:03:49.636 --> 00:03:52.370
So the moment that I read
that, I close my laptop

00:03:52.370 --> 00:03:55.348
and this is what shifted
in me, three huge things.

00:03:55.348 --> 00:03:59.015
First, I spent the last 12
years studying vulnerability,

00:03:59.015 --> 00:04:03.192
and that quote was everything
I know about vulnerability.

00:04:03.192 --> 00:04:06.826
It is not about winning,
it's not about losing,

00:04:06.826 --> 00:04:09.909
it's about showing up and being seen.

00:04:10.876 --> 00:04:14.459
The second thing, this
is who I want to be.

00:04:15.700 --> 00:04:18.475
I want to create, I want to make things

00:04:18.475 --> 00:04:21.122
that didn't exist before I touched them.

00:04:21.122 --> 00:04:25.768
I want to show up and be seen
in my work and in my life.

00:04:25.768 --> 00:04:28.755
And if you're going to
show up and be seen,

00:04:28.755 --> 00:04:31.598
there's only one guarantee and that is

00:04:31.598 --> 00:04:34.491
you will get your ass kicked.

00:04:34.491 --> 00:04:37.169
That is the guarantee, that is
the only certainty you have.

00:04:37.169 --> 00:04:39.862
If you're going to go in the
arena and spend any time in there

00:04:39.862 --> 00:04:44.044
whatsoever, especially if
you've committed to creating

00:04:44.044 --> 00:04:46.598
in your life, you will
get your ass kicked.

00:04:46.598 --> 00:04:48.555
So you have to decide at that moment,

00:04:48.555 --> 00:04:52.397
I think for all of us, if
courage is a value that we hold,

00:04:52.397 --> 00:04:56.503
this is a consequence, you can't avoid it.

00:04:56.503 --> 00:04:59.173
The third thing, which really set me free

00:04:59.173 --> 00:05:01.130
and I think Steve my husband would argue

00:05:01.130 --> 00:05:03.912
has made me somewhat dangerous

00:05:03.912 --> 00:05:08.572
is kind of the new philosophy
about criticism which is this:

00:05:08.572 --> 00:05:12.107
if you're not in the arena
also getting your ass kicked,

00:05:12.107 --> 00:05:15.182
I'm not interested in
your feedback, period.

00:05:15.182 --> 00:05:17.732
(audience applauds)

00:05:17.732 --> 00:05:19.522
- What are the hardest parts
about being an entrepreneur

00:05:19.522 --> 00:05:23.503
is you put your idea out
there and it gets rejected.

00:05:23.503 --> 00:05:25.234
It doesn't work.

00:05:25.234 --> 00:05:29.201
Much more worrisome
than failing for people

00:05:29.201 --> 00:05:31.084
is failing in front of other people,

00:05:31.084 --> 00:05:33.751
to have this new product you create,

00:05:33.751 --> 00:05:36.504
or new service you create,
and you put it out there,

00:05:36.504 --> 00:05:39.314
and you don't get customers or even worse,

00:05:39.314 --> 00:05:42.095
your friends and your
family or people around you

00:05:42.095 --> 00:05:43.699
tell you it's never going to work out,

00:05:43.699 --> 00:05:46.472
and then it doesn't and then
you failed in front of them.

00:05:46.472 --> 00:05:49.543
And most people are so
afraid of that failure,

00:05:49.543 --> 00:05:52.610
of failing in front of
people that they care about,

00:05:52.610 --> 00:05:54.713
that they don't do anything.

00:05:54.713 --> 00:05:56.777
Because you have this plan,
this thing that you want to do,

00:05:56.777 --> 00:05:58.649
this great idea that you think
is going to change your life

00:05:58.649 --> 00:06:00.378
and help the people around you,

00:06:00.378 --> 00:06:02.440
but because it may not work out,

00:06:02.440 --> 00:06:05.320
because you don't have the
certainty that it's going to work,

00:06:05.320 --> 00:06:08.281
you play small and you
don't do anything about it.

00:06:08.281 --> 00:06:11.447
And there has to be a
point that you decide

00:06:11.447 --> 00:06:13.981
whether you are going to live

00:06:13.981 --> 00:06:16.672
according to your own
expectations or somebody else's.

00:06:16.672 --> 00:06:18.817
Like how long are you willing to let

00:06:18.817 --> 00:06:20.886
other people's opinions
and perspectives of you

00:06:20.886 --> 00:06:24.288
hold you back from doing the
thing that you want to do?

00:06:24.288 --> 00:06:26.070
A lot of times those perspectives

00:06:26.070 --> 00:06:27.360
and opinions will be wrong,

00:06:27.360 --> 00:06:28.749
a lot of times your friends

00:06:28.749 --> 00:06:30.282
and family are actually cheering you on,

00:06:30.282 --> 00:06:33.337
you still just don't want to
fail in front of other people,

00:06:33.337 --> 00:06:35.172
but sometimes is may be true.

00:06:35.172 --> 00:06:36.954
Sometimes your Uncle Joe will say,

00:06:36.954 --> 00:06:39.299
"You're never going to
make it, look at you,

00:06:39.299 --> 00:06:41.017
"look at your education
and your background,

00:06:41.017 --> 00:06:42.651
"and your family or how
much money you have.

00:06:42.651 --> 00:06:44.804
"You don't have the skills to do that."

00:06:44.804 --> 00:06:46.073
And he may be right.

00:06:46.073 --> 00:06:50.301
But you won't know until you
actually go out and test it.

00:06:50.301 --> 00:06:52.851
And I relate and I resonate.

00:06:52.851 --> 00:06:57.407
In my first business when
I was making $300 a month,

00:06:57.407 --> 00:06:59.746
I turned down the high-paying
jobs that I thought I wanted,

00:06:59.746 --> 00:07:01.741
that my friends all wanted, and

00:07:01.741 --> 00:07:05.183
I was too embarrassed and
ashamed to tell my friends

00:07:05.183 --> 00:07:07.714
that I had no money, that
I couldn't go out to beer

00:07:07.714 --> 00:07:10.408
and grab, you know, beer
and pizza with them.

00:07:10.408 --> 00:07:12.513
And I had to pick one thing
month that I could go to,

00:07:12.513 --> 00:07:13.841
'cause that's all I could afford.

00:07:13.841 --> 00:07:16.173
But I was too embarrassed
and ashamed to tell them.

00:07:16.173 --> 00:07:18.419
When they asked how I
was doing, I would say,

00:07:18.419 --> 00:07:20.274
you know, I'm living the
entrepreneur lifestyle,

00:07:20.274 --> 00:07:21.970
everything's great,
I'm just hustling hard,

00:07:21.970 --> 00:07:23.481
I'm working, I'm working.

00:07:23.481 --> 00:07:26.208
But really I was just, I
couldn't afford to go out.

00:07:26.208 --> 00:07:29.119
And I'm sure if I actually told them that,

00:07:29.119 --> 00:07:32.287
they would understand, and
they would have my back,

00:07:32.287 --> 00:07:34.435
and they would've been
supportive and encouraging.

00:07:34.435 --> 00:07:35.859
Maybe some of them would've razzed me,

00:07:35.859 --> 00:07:38.371
but I think that they
would've supported me.

00:07:38.371 --> 00:07:40.693
And that would've actually
been very helpful to me,

00:07:40.693 --> 00:07:42.895
'cause at the time I was dealing
with everything by myself.

00:07:42.895 --> 00:07:44.696
I was trying to internalize everything,

00:07:44.696 --> 00:07:48.454
and to the outside world,
be seen as a success.

00:07:48.454 --> 00:07:52.096
I think about my friend
who really wanted to get

00:07:52.096 --> 00:07:53.800
in front of the camera.

00:07:53.800 --> 00:07:55.753
He was a guy who was behind
the camera all the time,

00:07:55.753 --> 00:07:57.481
and he wanted to be in
front of the camera.

00:07:57.481 --> 00:07:59.493
And one day I forced him,

00:07:59.493 --> 00:08:01.958
I pushed him to be in front of the camera.

00:08:01.958 --> 00:08:04.414
And I asked him, why are you so afraid

00:08:04.414 --> 00:08:05.610
to be in front of the camera?

00:08:05.610 --> 00:08:07.829
You want to do this, like
you want to spread a message.

00:08:07.829 --> 00:08:10.449
Why are you so afraid to
get in front of the camera?

00:08:10.449 --> 00:08:12.872
He was worried about what
his friends would say

00:08:12.872 --> 00:08:15.271
on Facebook if they saw a video of him,

00:08:15.271 --> 00:08:17.022
he's worried there'd be a negative vibe,

00:08:17.022 --> 00:08:18.692
he's worried they wouldn't support him,

00:08:18.692 --> 00:08:21.972
and so I did something dramatic.

00:08:21.972 --> 00:08:24.399
You know, I filmed him,
I said, enough of this,

00:08:24.399 --> 00:08:25.917
we're going to film you,
we're going to put you

00:08:25.917 --> 00:08:27.156
in front of the camera.

00:08:27.156 --> 00:08:29.273
I put him in front of the
camera and he shared his message

00:08:29.273 --> 00:08:33.440
and then I posted the video
and I posted it to Facebook

00:08:34.405 --> 00:08:38.487
and I tagged him and I
contacted his wife, and

00:08:38.487 --> 00:08:40.811
I had her contact all of his friends

00:08:40.811 --> 00:08:42.663
who I didn't have as mutual friends,

00:08:42.663 --> 00:08:44.394
and say, hey, watch this video.

00:08:44.394 --> 00:08:46.210
And something amazing happened.

00:08:46.210 --> 00:08:48.611
All of his friends were super supportive,

00:08:48.611 --> 00:08:50.395
were encouraging him,
were cheering him on,

00:08:50.395 --> 00:08:52.458
where he thought there'd
be this negative buzz,

00:08:52.458 --> 00:08:53.775
negative vibe, judgment,

00:08:53.775 --> 00:08:57.971
a lot of negativity, and
it was the exact opposite.

00:08:57.971 --> 00:09:01.163
They supported him and wanted
him to go and have success.

00:09:01.163 --> 00:09:03.749
And when he saw that difference,

00:09:03.749 --> 00:09:06.483
that sparked a shift for him.

00:09:06.483 --> 00:09:10.413
And then he started getting
in front of the camera.

00:09:10.413 --> 00:09:12.243
And he's been unafraid to get

00:09:12.243 --> 00:09:14.763
in front of the camera ever since.

00:09:14.763 --> 00:09:17.108
He's created a lot of
interviews, a lot of videos,

00:09:17.108 --> 00:09:20.003
a lot of moving videos, some
with me, some with others,

00:09:20.003 --> 00:09:23.222
where now he enjoys being
in front of the camera.

00:09:23.222 --> 00:09:26.249
Just because he was living
according to what he thought

00:09:26.249 --> 00:09:29.552
his friends would think, and
experiencing their support

00:09:29.552 --> 00:09:31.835
and kind of being pushed
into the limelight

00:09:31.835 --> 00:09:33.639
made that shift for him.

00:09:33.639 --> 00:09:35.332
But I said it was going
to work out like that.

00:09:35.332 --> 00:09:38.083
Sometimes you will fall flat on your face.

00:09:38.083 --> 00:09:40.225
Sometimes people may laugh at you,

00:09:40.225 --> 00:09:42.245
sometimes the people in
your network will tell you

00:09:42.245 --> 00:09:44.229
that you suck and that you're
never going to be a success.

00:09:44.229 --> 00:09:48.584
You just have to decide
at what point in your life

00:09:48.584 --> 00:09:50.701
are you going to show up and do the thing

00:09:50.701 --> 00:09:53.211
that you want to do and get a result

00:09:53.211 --> 00:09:57.073
and just see if it works,
versus just sitting in your head

00:09:57.073 --> 00:09:58.854
all day wishing you could do something,

00:09:58.854 --> 00:10:01.512
but being afraid because of other people's

00:10:01.512 --> 00:10:03.905
expectations and perceptions.

00:10:03.905 --> 00:10:05.757
At some point you have to say,

00:10:05.757 --> 00:10:07.698
I've had enough.

00:10:07.698 --> 00:10:10.411
I don't care what you guys think.

00:10:10.411 --> 00:10:12.609
I'm going to go out and do it,

00:10:12.609 --> 00:10:15.063
because I need to prove
to myself that I can,

00:10:15.063 --> 00:10:17.221
or at least I need certainty that I can't.

00:10:17.221 --> 00:10:19.008
So the question today is I'm curious

00:10:19.008 --> 00:10:21.789
what has prevented you
from truly showing up?

00:10:21.789 --> 00:10:24.569
From really releasing the
message or the product

00:10:24.569 --> 00:10:26.731
or service, or the business
that you have inside you,

00:10:26.731 --> 00:10:29.910
what has prevented you from
really going all at it?

00:10:29.910 --> 00:10:31.953
What are you so afraid of?

00:10:31.953 --> 00:10:33.699
Leave it down in the comments below,

00:10:33.699 --> 00:10:35.170
I'm really curious to find out.

00:10:35.170 --> 00:10:36.882
And if you leave a comment
within the first couple of hours

00:10:36.882 --> 00:10:38.729
of the video going live,
you have a good chance

00:10:38.729 --> 00:10:41.332
of winning one of our two daily prizes.

00:10:41.332 --> 00:10:43.037
I also want to give a
quick shout out to Mary.

00:10:43.037 --> 00:10:45.312
Mary, thank you so much for
picking up a copy of my book,

00:10:45.312 --> 00:10:47.200
Your One Word and taking that picture,

00:10:47.200 --> 00:10:49.075
it looks great leaning
up against your laptop.

00:10:49.075 --> 00:10:50.803
I hope you enjoyed the book,

00:10:50.803 --> 00:10:52.870
and I really appreciate your support.

00:10:52.870 --> 00:10:54.325
Thank you guys again for watching,

00:10:54.325 --> 00:10:55.900
I believe in you, I hope you continue

00:10:55.900 --> 00:10:58.379
to believe in yourself and
whatever your one word is,

00:10:58.379 --> 00:11:01.301
much love and I'll see
you again tomorrow morning

00:11:01.301 --> 00:11:04.060
for another shot of Entspresso.

00:11:04.060 --> 00:11:06.047
♫ I wake up every morning

00:11:06.047 --> 00:11:09.464
♫ Espresso keep me going

00:11:13.048 --> 00:11:13.881
- I had a path.

00:11:13.881 --> 00:11:15.153
I knew where my path was.

00:11:15.153 --> 00:11:18.528
My path was to become what I am right now.

00:11:18.528 --> 00:11:21.508
Now, I lost sight of it in
an interesting sort of way

00:11:21.508 --> 00:11:23.008
or I went about it

00:11:25.374 --> 00:11:27.420
in a wayward path.

00:11:27.420 --> 00:11:31.810
But fortunately for me,
all the getting high,

00:11:31.810 --> 00:11:34.719
the drinking, the drugs,
everything else I did,

00:11:34.719 --> 00:11:37.694
I showed up at the theater every day.

00:11:37.694 --> 00:11:40.850
I did plays, ripped out of my mind,

00:11:40.850 --> 00:11:43.199
I rehearsed, ripped out of my mind,

00:11:43.199 --> 00:11:45.916
but every lesson that I learned,

00:11:45.916 --> 00:11:47.638
I held on to for some reason.

00:11:47.638 --> 00:11:50.537
God, whatever, somebody let me hold on

00:11:50.537 --> 00:11:52.176
to everything that I was learning.

00:11:52.176 --> 00:11:54.097
My stage lefts, my stage rights,

00:11:54.097 --> 00:11:58.072
my upstage foot always
out, turn down this way,

00:11:58.072 --> 00:11:59.839
learning how to develop a character,

00:11:59.839 --> 00:12:00.891
doing all those things,

00:12:00.891 --> 00:12:02.348
because those are the things that I love.

00:12:02.348 --> 00:12:05.100
And I did them in the
midst of everything else

00:12:05.100 --> 00:12:06.149
that I was doing to,

00:12:06.149 --> 00:12:08.683
you know, when my friends
were getting ready

00:12:08.683 --> 00:12:10.109
to go get some more drugs, I go,

00:12:10.109 --> 00:12:11.522
and I got to be at the theater.

00:12:11.522 --> 00:12:13.848
And I'll catch you all when
the theater's over, you know,

00:12:13.848 --> 00:12:15.517
when I'm done, and I'd shew, I'd jet.

00:12:15.517 --> 00:12:17.478
Or I got to go build a
set, I got to do this.

00:12:17.478 --> 00:12:19.219
So I did everything that I had to do.

00:12:19.219 --> 00:12:22.495
So I was focused on this
by any means necessary.

00:12:22.495 --> 00:12:24.620
Plus I had a professor
who was like, you know,

00:12:24.620 --> 00:12:26.876
well, you know, all the
great ones do their jobs

00:12:26.876 --> 00:12:28.579
and they ripped out of the their minds.

00:12:28.579 --> 00:12:30.143
You know, you look at the Peter O'Tools,

00:12:30.143 --> 00:12:31.952
and the da da da da, da da da, you know,

00:12:31.952 --> 00:12:33.596
they get drunk, they get
high, they do what they do,

00:12:33.596 --> 00:12:35.423
but they show up and they do their jobs.

00:12:35.423 --> 00:12:36.837
So we were like, okay.

00:12:36.837 --> 00:12:39.566
And that's what we did, you
know, we drank with him,

00:12:39.566 --> 00:12:41.946
and we went to Styles Acting class.

00:12:41.946 --> 00:12:44.639
We'd go smoke a joint and come in

00:12:44.639 --> 00:12:46.060
and do our other acting classes,

00:12:46.060 --> 00:12:47.723
or go build a set, or build some costumes,

00:12:47.723 --> 00:12:49.243
or hang some lights and do all the things

00:12:49.243 --> 00:12:50.410
that we had to do.

00:12:50.410 --> 00:12:53.608
So I kept learning my
lessons and doing them.

00:12:53.608 --> 00:12:57.085
- In different places
in life, I promise you,

00:12:57.085 --> 00:13:00.835
you're going to find you
don't know where to go.

00:13:02.181 --> 00:13:03.658
Everybody goes through this.

00:13:03.658 --> 00:13:05.934
The most successful people
in the world wake up

00:13:05.934 --> 00:13:09.601
some mornings with no
clue what to do today.

00:13:11.247 --> 00:13:13.109
Okay, so first thing I want you to know

00:13:13.109 --> 00:13:15.521
is that it's normal, it
happens to everybody.

00:13:15.521 --> 00:13:17.010
It's not like you're a bad person

00:13:17.010 --> 00:13:18.667
or you're lost or you're depressed

00:13:18.667 --> 00:13:22.532
or you got some problem you
need to take medication for.

00:13:22.532 --> 00:13:27.240
Everybody, everybody regardless
of their stature in life,

00:13:27.240 --> 00:13:29.331
where they are, regardless of their money,

00:13:29.331 --> 00:13:30.961
their relationship,

00:13:30.961 --> 00:13:33.461
their job, they run the joint,

00:13:35.597 --> 00:13:38.995
promise you, no matter
how much they present

00:13:38.995 --> 00:13:43.331
like they look like got the
whole package put together,

00:13:43.331 --> 00:13:46.331
everybody, everybody has those days,

00:13:48.351 --> 00:13:50.550
and the sun is kicking today,

00:13:50.550 --> 00:13:52.217
has those days where

00:13:55.182 --> 00:13:57.432
they don't know what to do.

00:13:58.764 --> 00:14:01.135
I don't know what to do, you know?

00:14:01.135 --> 00:14:02.381
Uncertainty.

00:14:02.381 --> 00:14:03.902
My friends Dale Christenson told me

00:14:03.902 --> 00:14:05.585
when I was 25 years old.

00:14:05.585 --> 00:14:07.613
I was experiencing depression every day,

00:14:07.613 --> 00:14:12.215
he's like, no matter
what, man, no matter what,

00:14:12.215 --> 00:14:14.229
no matter what, dude, show up.

00:14:14.229 --> 00:14:17.038
Even if your eyes are bleeding, show up.

00:14:17.038 --> 00:14:19.001
I've been doing that for 34 years now.

00:14:19.001 --> 00:14:22.269
Show up, even when I don't want to, okay.

00:14:22.269 --> 00:14:23.567
And then what I try to do is

00:14:23.567 --> 00:14:27.288
I try to help one person, one person.

00:14:27.288 --> 00:14:30.257
And what happened over
the period of 34 years,

00:14:30.257 --> 00:14:31.625
I did that every day.

00:14:31.625 --> 00:14:33.254
I'm not depressed anymore,

00:14:33.254 --> 00:14:34.930
at least not for long periods of time.

00:14:34.930 --> 00:14:36.475
I don't use any kind of medication,

00:14:36.475 --> 00:14:37.928
don't use any kind of drugs.

00:14:37.928 --> 00:14:41.079
Don't smoke weed, don't
drink over excessively drink,

00:14:41.079 --> 00:14:43.625
I might have drink once in a while.

00:14:43.625 --> 00:14:46.489
And got a beautiful
wife, two beautiful kids,

00:14:46.489 --> 00:14:48.573
and for the most part my
life is freaking wonderful.

00:14:48.573 --> 00:14:50.473
All I did was this.

00:14:50.473 --> 00:14:52.265
I don't over analyze,

00:14:52.265 --> 00:14:55.848
never do I label myself
a loser, a quitter.

00:14:59.107 --> 00:15:00.574
I'm hard on myself.

00:15:00.574 --> 00:15:03.991
I never label myself OCD, ACD, ADD, OCDD,

00:15:07.008 --> 00:15:10.001
whatever a depressant, alcohol,

00:15:10.001 --> 00:15:11.580
like a drug addict, no, no, I don't.

00:15:11.580 --> 00:15:13.326
This is what I do, I do things, okay.

00:15:13.326 --> 00:15:15.003
I show up, move in the direction,

00:15:15.003 --> 00:15:17.178
I don't overanalyze, move in the direction

00:15:17.178 --> 00:15:20.812
that I think could be more pro survival

00:15:20.812 --> 00:15:22.245
than staying in one place.

00:15:22.245 --> 00:15:24.429
And number three, help somebody.

